1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:05,150
易考范文十一

2
00:00:05,159 --> 00:00:08,730
In the ridiculous cartoon,

3
00:00:08,739 --> 00:00:12,840
a man is peering into a telescope with great interest,

4
00:00:12,849 --> 00:00:16,120
a half-naked woman emerging in his mind.

5
00:00:16,129 --> 00:00:22,030
Behind him a long queue of men are waiting for their turn in eager anticipation.

6
00:00:22,039 --> 00:00:27,670
A couple of words—certain social surveys—can be seen on the telescope.

7
00:00:27,679 --> 00:00:31,600
The cartoon aims to highlight a social aspect

8
00:00:31,609 --> 00:00:36,340
that a bundle of surveys pay excessive attention to personal privacy.

9
00:00:36,349 --> 00:00:39,060
Who is to blame for the phenomenon?

10
00:00:39,069 --> 00:00:43,720
In my opinion, the media are mainly responsible for it.

11
00:00:43,729 --> 00:00:47,490
 A good social survey is supposed to provide insight into

12
00:00:47,499 --> 00:00:52,870
some general matters of the society and appeal to people for concern about them.

13
00:00:52,879 --> 00:00:58,550
 However, the media, who conduct most social surveys,

14
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:04,160
are more interested in privacy-related issues than in widespread problems.

15
00:01:04,169 --> 00:01:08,590
 Trying to please the public with claptrap and gain fame,

16
00:01:08,599 --> 00:01:13,470
the media actually mislead the public, and, purposely sometimes,

17
00:01:13,479 --> 00:01:16,380
infringe on citizens' right of privacy.

18
00:01:16,389 --> 00:01:18,560
As far as I am concerned,

19
00:01:18,569 --> 00:01:23,290
the solution lies in the joint effort of the authorities and the media.

20
00:01:23,299 --> 00:01:25,990
On the one hand, it is essential that

21
00:01:25,999 --> 00:01:29,710
the authorities formulate laws and regulations to ensure

22
00:01:29,719 --> 00:01:33,210
that individual information is kept confidential.

23
00:01:33,219 --> 00:01:38,730
On the other hand, the media must strengthen their sense of social responsibility,

24
00:01:38,739 --> 00:01:40,730
directing the public’s attention to issues of more significance.

